-- ===========================================================================
-- Generated by drizzle-kit, then annotated. The statement is the generated one.
--
-- committed_date becomes nullable — decision F8, and the ONLY point at which
-- Phase 2 relaxes spec section 10.
--
-- A historical job copied out of a paper book genuinely has no commitment
-- recorded against it. Writing an invented date would be worse than writing
-- none: an invented date is indistinguishable from a real one, and would
-- quietly become part of OTD, the single number this system exists to produce.
--
-- This ALTER is safe only in company with 0006, which:
--   - excludes null-committed rows from v_otd entirely, so they are never
--     counted as met and never counted as missed;
--   - reports is_overdue and is_at_risk as FALSE rather than NULL for them.
--
-- And in company with the application rules, which do not live in SQL:
--   - the PO capture form requires a committed date, always;
--   - the importer is the only path permitted to write null;
--   - screens render null as "Historical — no commitment recorded".
-- ===========================================================================

ALTER TABLE "po_item" ALTER COLUMN "committed_date" DROP NOT NULL;
